Source: https://github.com/BryanLunduke/lundukecity2

Lunduke City 2 is a city-building game. Its simulation engine is the
Micropolis engine (GPL-3.0-or-later) with the additional terms below,
modified by Lunduke City 2. The user interface (SDL3 for windows, input
and audio; Cairo and Pango for drawing and text) is original to Lunduke
City 2 and is also GPL-3.0-or-later. The complete GNU GPL version 3 is in
the file COPYING.

This tree does not include the upstream Tcl/Tk interface, Python/SWIG
bindings, or scenario files. DejaVu Serif (Year in Review titles) is
vendored under data/fonts; the Windows package still adds DejaVu Sans
and Sans Mono from the toolchain. Map tiles, sprites, the
hexa tile resources, and sounds are vendored separately (see below).
The additional terms apply to the engine sources, to those assets, and
to the combined program.

In this copyright file the last matching Files paragraph wins, so the
specific vendored paths are listed after the general paragraph.

